      "content": "That's incredible, but very concerning. It's quite rare for a single entity to have access across different platforms, unless you've been sharing your same or similar usernames and passwords. It might be worth taking a closer look at which accounts you're using and whether there could be a connection between them. It's best to consider setting up strong, unique passwords for different sites and using a password manager. Additionally, look for any security questions or unforeseen links that may have compromised your other accounts. You could also check for any recent data breaches or public records that may link you to other accounts, potentially explaining the pattern of deletions. Lastly, discuss this issue with a cybersecurity professional for a thorough investigation.",
